    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0366" n="326" xml:id="pg326"/>

                <head>165. Telegram From the Department of State to the Legation in Hungary<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d165-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-04-06T18:48:00-05:00">April 6, 1961,
                            6:48 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>269. Zorin announced in Political Committee April 5 USSR would not press U–2,
                    RB–47 complaint against US and suggested states concerned take steps clear
                    agenda of Hungary and Tibet. Yost welcomed Zorin’s statement re U–2 and RB–47
                    case but observed Hungary and Tibet not in same category. Later, spokesman USDel
                    informed press US not prepared drop Hungary and Tibet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
